A||N||11||jhogans||Subwoofer encloser question||||5||
Z||000000||jhogans||12-07-1999||02:30 PM||||What size is the woofer?  What is the internal volume of the subwoofer enclosure?  I know a company that makes 5" SUBWOOFERS.  Not woofers but SUBWOOFERS.  It is made by FOCAL.  If the factory subwoofer is a 6.5" inch speaker than I can cut some wood and fit the 5" SUB.<P>Thanks for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ditz88GT||12-07-1999||03:19 PM||||I think the speaker was a 5.25 midwooofer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jhogans||12-07-1999||03:35 PM||||5.25 will be perfect.  All I need to do is make an adapter plate to fit the 5" sub.  Now what is the internal volume?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ditz88GT||12-07-1999||05:51 PM||||??????????????????????<BR>Now that I'm unsure of.<BR>??????????????????????||||reg||5
Z||000004||geyser||12-07-1999||06:18 PM||||The Fiero subwoofer is in a ported reflex enclosure. This would be different than just building a box for a speaker. Most woofers, specifically subwoofers, are designed to be mounted in an engineered box of basically two types;  acoustic suspension (a totally sealed box of a given volume), or ported reflex (sealed box of a given volume with a cylindrical port allowing the box to breathe).  The spec sheet that came with the speaker should give you the info you will need to calculate the enclosure and,  if used,  the port size and length. Find 1. free air resonance; 2.  Q(ts); and 3. V(as). Don't worry about what these mean, just see if the spec sheet lists these. If not we can still come up with something. Get back to me.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jhogans||12-09-1999||04:50 AM||||Does anybody know the internal volume of the factory subwoofer box.||||reg||1
Z||000006||jhogans||12-09-1999||04:52 AM||||How do I remove the subwoofer box?||||reg||1
Z||000007||JetroGT||12-09-1999||05:02 AM||||That's easy. Use a metric 10 and a 7 socket. Unbolt it and it just drops down.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jhogans||12-09-1999||05:15 AM||||Thanks for all of the info guys.  I will check out the box in the morning and guesstimate the internal volume.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||12-09-1999||09:15 AM||||You could fill it with water and then dump the water into a container with measuring marks on it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||12-09-1999||10:48 AM||||Sand would be dryer||||reg||1
Z||000011||jhogans||12-09-1999||11:26 AM||||Gotcha.  I forgot the good old water and sand.  Thanks.||||reg||1
